Question: Book of the dead.

The first time I killed the Wizard of Yendor, he was standing over the moat.
So the Book fell in the moat. I didn't know that the book was in the moat,
so I continued all the way down to level 56 without the book, I knew that
I would get the book from the Wizard but after killing him 5-7 times on my 
way down, I decided to come back to the level where I killed the wizard the
first time. When I entered the level where I killed the Wizard the 1st time,
the game said something like: "Steam rises from the papyrus spellbook",
in fact the game said the same thing when I saved the game and also when
I loaded my saved game, regardless to on what level I were. IS THERE
SOMETHING WRONG IN THE CODE, or why did it say the "steam rises..." when
I saved or loaded the game AND I wasn't on the level where the Book was 
lying in the moat? Next I had to get the book from the moat, but traveling
down all the way to level 56 and back, I didn't remember in which moat 
square the Book were. My character had water walking boots. So I tried to
pick up things while standing over the moat there were two kinds of 
'answers' the game gave me : 1. 'There is nothing here to pick up.' and
2. 'You cannot dive into the water to pick things up.'. So after checking
the moat squares I knew in which square the Book was lying. (I got the
answer #2, I just mentioned.) I didn't have an amulet of magical breathing,
because of polypiling (I wanted more life saving amulets), but I had
both polymorph and polymorph control rings. I turned into a crocodile, but
I did't see anything it that square nor get anything up, next I tried as
a water elemental, but still nothing. WHYCOME WATER MONSTERS CAN'T PICK
THINGS UP WHILE IN WATER SQUARE? Well luckily I knew teleport spell (a wand
would've done the same) so I teleported the Book out from the moat. Next I
searched the whole level and got the Book.

Questions : crashes...

I proceeded down to level 56, made the ritual, and nailed the High Priest.
Less than 10 moves after I had picked the Amulet of Yendor the game crashed
saying: 'Segmentation fault'. WHAT MIGHT MAKE THIS HAPPEN? After a succesful
recovery, I continued playing, (I had to play that level once more). I came
all the way back up to level 1 and proceeded to Endgame. IS IT A FEATURE IN
THE GEHENNON LEVELS WHEN YOU HAVE THE AMULET OF YENDOR, THAT WHEN YOU CLIMB
UP A LEVEL, YOU MIGHT BE TRANSFERRED 1 TO 2 LEVELS DOWNWARDS? Anyway, on
Earth Plane, nothing unusual happened, but in Air Plane I got my second
'Segmentation fault' error after kicking a monster to get me to move into
the opposite direction. (I didn't have a levitation ring...) So I had to
run that recover program again... and in Fire Plane things got really weird.
While in the Fire Plane the game hanged itself, I mean the game just got
frozen. No commands did go through to the game. I had to go to another
terminal and Kill my Nethack process from there, with -HUP option. That
saved my game, then I reloaded it and continued playing. This 'game frozen'
thing happened totally about 20 times. I noticed it usually to happen
when I just got the killing blow to a monster. ANY GUESSES WHY MY GAME
GOT FROZEN? A couple of these 'game frozen' things also happened in the 
Water Plane, but not many (4-5 if I remember right). And at last I got myself
to the Astral Plane, where I met my third 'Segmentation fault'.
After I recovered that one I finally ascended to Demigod-Hood.
WHAT WERE ALL THOSE 'GAME FROZEN' THINGS ALL ABOUT?

